  "note": "Poll on Wednesday 20 May 1964: thirteen candidates for nine seats, all Independents (Belfast Telegraph, 21 May 1964). 598 ratepayers voted, more than 80 per cent. Tom Hutchinson, a former chairman, Amos Stewart and William F. Gillespie lost their seats; M. McKinney is Mervyn McKinney, standing for the first time. Returning officer William Mayes. The Belfast Telegraph's list prints Ryans's vote as 453 (text, not checked on the image); the local paper's figure is used."
